[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2.g3"]
[Start "1. c4 Nf6"]

2. g3 ( 2. Nf3 e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 Be7 ) 2... e6 { The same setup as always. White's bishop will aim at d5 and b7, so Black wants a solid pawn on d5. } 3. Bg2 d5 { Takes the centre. If White captures on d5 Black recaptures with the e-pawn and blocks the g2 bishop. } 4. cxd5 ( 4. d4 Be7 5. Nf3 O-O ) ( 4. Nf3 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. b3 c5 7. Bb2 Nc6 ) 4... exd5 { Keeps a pawn on d5, where it also shuts the g2 bishop out of the game. } 5. Nf3 Be7 { Clears f8 so Black can castle; the d5 pawn is guarded by the knight and the queen. } 6. O-O O-O 7. d4 c6 { Guards d5 for good, so the g2 bishop has nothing to look at. The queen also gets c7 or b6. } 8. Nc3 Nbd7 { Develops the last knight. Plan: ...Re8, ...Nf8-e6 or ...Nb6, and keep the c6 and d5 pawns together. } *
